| info        = 
*Khora commands her loyal [[Kavat]] companion {{Companion|Venari}} to prioritize a target on the aiming reticle for {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''25''' [[energy]], leaving Venari's mark above the target for <u>'''120'''</u> seconds. Once commanded, Venari chases the marked target if nearby or teleports to it if far away, while refreshing the special effect for her battle posture if it is on cooldown. When Venari reaches the target, she will perform different tasks depending on her battle posture.
**The target is marked by a floating battle posture icon above their head.
**Venari's mark cannot be recast on the same target while it is still active.
**Venari's mark lasts until its duration expires, Khora marks a different target, Venari's battle posture is switched, or the target dies.
**Marked targets are prioritized by Venari over enemies afflicted by {{D|Slash}} with {{M|Hunter Command}} equipped.
**Venari will teleport to marked targets that are more than <u>'''15'''</u> meters away from Khora, even after the mark is initially applied.
**When a target is marked, Venari audibly snarls in response.
*While Venari is alive, Khora passively gains a {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''5% / 10% / 12.5% / 15%''' [[Movement Speed]] bonus.
*When Venari is killed, she will respawn beside Khora after <u>'''45'''</u> seconds, displayed on the ability icon. Casting this ability while Venari is dead will instead spend up to {{Stat|Ability Efficiency|icon=only}}'''50''' Energy to revive her instantly.
**Venari's battle posture cannot be switched while she is dead.
**Revive Energy cost is proportional to the remaining time until Venari is revived naturally: the less time remains, the less the revive will cost.
**Respawn time is '''not''' affected by mods.
**Effects that reduce Recovery Time (such as {{M|Tenacious Bond}}) will not reduce Venari's respawn time.
**Venari disappears completely while dead, and cannot be revived through normal means.
**Venari appears next to Khora upon respawning.
*All postures are available by default when Venari is unlocked at Warframe rank '''5'''.
*Holding the ability key (default {{Keybind|3}}) cycles to Venari's next battle posture for no energy cost, and also deactivates any current Mark:
<div class="tabber-borderless" ><tabber>
|-| Attack =
*Khora commands Venari to adopt her '''Attack''' posture, causing her to ferociously assault nearby enemies and allowing her to use '''Snare'''. During Snare, Venari chains her chosen target in place for <u>'''2.5'''</u> seconds, as she damages the target with '''5''' hits over the course of the animation; each hit inflicts {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''350''' {{D|Slash}} damage with a guaranteed [[Status Effect]] proc. Snare has a cooldown of <u>'''3'''</u> seconds, which can be bypassed by Khora manually marking a target.
**Snare damage is affected by {{M|Maul}}, {{M|Venom Teeth}} and other elemental damage mods.
**Snare damage type is affected by elemental mods, including {{M|Venom Teeth}}, {{M|Shock Collar}}, {{M|Flame Gland}}, and {{M|Frost Jaw}}.
**Snare is capable of inflicting [[Status Effect|Status Effects]] with every hit in addition to the forced {{D|Slash}} Status Effect. It inherits Venari's Status Chance and damage spread shown on the [[Arsenal]] as normal.
**Snare has '''0%''' critical chance and is '''not''' affected by {{M|Bite}} or {{M|Hunter Synergy}}.
**Venari's Attack mark can only be cast on an enemy target.
**Venari's Attack mark will remain on the target until it expires, allowing Venari to focus on killing the target with multiple Snare attacks.
*Snare is '''not''' affected by {{M|Swipe}}'s multiple targeting and range extension.
*Casting Snare is a full-body animation that causes Venari to maneuver around the target, before reappearing near the target once finished.
*Venari is still vulnerable to damage while performing her special attack animation.
*During Snare, the target is visually held in place by living chains that attach to nearby surfaces.

|-| Protect = 
*Khora commands Venari to adopt her '''Protect''' posture, causing her to defend Khora or herself from the nearest enemy and allowing her to use '''Tail Whip'''. During Tail Whip, Venari spins in place to inflict {{D|Knockdown}} and {{D|Disarmed}} on a single enemy. Tail Whip has a cooldown of <u>'''3'''</u> seconds, which can be bypassed by Khora manually marking a target.
**Tail Whip will affect the target even if it moves away from Venari during her spin animation.
**Does '''not''' knockdown nor disarm enemies innately wielding melee weapons.
**Venari's Protect mark can only be cast on an enemy target.
**Venari's Protect mark is removed once Tail Whip is performed on the target.
*Casting Tail Whip is a full-body animation that stops Venari in place.

|-|Heal =
*Khora commands Venari to adopt her '''Heal''' posture, imbuing her with healing energy and allowing her to use '''Revitalize'''. When the current [[Health]] of any ally player in the squad or Venari herself reaches below <u>'''90%'''</u> of maximum health, Venari snarls and radiates a healing aura with a <u>'''10'''</u> meters radius; during Revitalize, Venari instinctively seeks out and follows the player with the lowest amount of current health, granting the target and any nearby injured allies {{Stat|Ability Strength|icon=only}}'''50''' health regen per second while they remain in the aura.
**Eligible targets for healing includes all Warframes, [[Companions]], [[Eidolon Lure]]s, summoned allied units such as [[Specter]]s, allied [[Invasion]] units, [[Rescue|Hostages]], [[Kavor Defector]]s, [[Sortie]] and [[Arbitrations]] Defense Operatives, and [[Defense Objects]].
**Venari's Heal does '''not''' affect [[Necramech]]s or [[Operator]]s.
**Revitalize deactivates when all allied players are above the missing health threshold.
**Revitalize does '''not''' grant [[Shield]] points.
**Venari's Heal mark can only be cast on an ally target.
**Venari's Heal mark is removed once Khora marks another target, the target is killed, or Khora switches battle posture.
*Venari will immediately activate Revitalize then follow the marked target, if Khora marks a target or herself by casting {{Keybind|3}} without a target on the aiming reticle. A quick and reliable way of marking Khora herself is to aim straight up briefly then casting the ability.
**Venari will closely follow its target and Revitalize will '''not''' deactivate until the mark is removed. While following a target, Venari also will '''not''' attack nearby enemies unless she is equipped with supplemental attack mods like {{M|Sharpened Claws}} or {{M|Pounce}}. 
*Khora can mark Venari to activate Revitalize, causing Venari to stand still at her current position for <u>'''65'''</u> seconds or until the mark is removed.
*{{M|Growing Power}} increases healing per second when Venari activates Revitalize during its effect; the bonus healing per second persists until Revitalize is deactivated.
*Activating Revitalize is a full-body animation that stops Venari in place, while deactivating Revitalize does '''not''' require an animation.
*While the healing aura is active, Venari and the affected allies glow in Khora's chosen energy color.

</tabber></div>
<hr />

*While Venari is in a neutral state with no active Marks she is far less likely to get stuck in terrain, frequently teleporting in beside you if you have gotten ahead of her.
*Casting Venari to apply a mark or revive her is a [[One-Handed Action]]. Swapping postures is an upper-body animation which does not restrict movement.
**The animations of this ability are not affected by [[Casting Speed]].
*Venari does '''not''' benefit from the set bonus of the [[Hunter Set]].
*[[Set Mods]] equipped on Venari do not count towards the number of mods equipped for the set bonus.
*{{M|Fetch}} equipped on Venari '''does not''' stack with {{M|Vacuum}} or {{M|Fetch}} equipped on companions.
*Khora's metallic adornments and Venari's tail change appearance depending on the selected posture: Attack (long spikes), Protect (small stubs and hammer tail), and Heal (curved blades).
*While Venari is dead, Khora's metallic adornments are hidden from view and will reappear once Venari respawns.
*The following visual effects are affected by Khora's chosen Warframe energy color:
**Venari's eye and regalia colors, mark icon color, as well as her death and respawn/teleport landing impact.
**Khora's battle posture switching.
**Attack posture Snare trails and Heal posture Revitalize glow.
